## 9. Flujo Completo — Escenario de Login a Endpoint Protegido

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor Cliente
    participant MW_Error as ErrorHandling MW
    participant MW_Log as Logging MW
    participant MW_Auth as SessionAuth MW
    participant Controller as SecurityController
    participant AuthCore as AuthNetCore
    participant BD as SQL Server

    Cliente->>MW_Error: POST /security/login { user, pass }
    MW_Error->>MW_Log: pasa la petición
    MW_Log->>MW_Auth: registra entrada
    MW_Auth->>MW_Auth: ¿Ruta pública? /security/login → SÍ
    MW_Auth->>Controller: pasa sin verificar sesión
    Controller->>AuthCore: Login(request, sessionKey)
    AuthCore->>BD: SELECT usuario + permisos
    BD-->>AuthCore: UserModel con permisos[]
    AuthCore-->>Controller: { SessionKey: "abc-123", User: {...} }
    Controller->>Controller: Session.SetString("sessionKey", "abc-123")
    Controller-->>Cliente: 200 OK { SessionKey, User }

    Note over Cliente: Segunda petición con sesión

    Cliente->>MW_Error: GET /user (cookie sessionKey=abc-123)
    MW_Error->>MW_Log: pasa la petición
    MW_Log->>MW_Auth: registra entrada
    MW_Auth->>AuthCore: Authenticate("abc-123")
    AuthCore-->>MW_Auth: true (sesión válida)
    MW_Auth->>Controller: pasa al UserController
    Controller->>Controller: [AuthController(CanViewUsers)] verifica permiso
    Controller->>AuthCore: HavePermission("abc-123", [CanViewUsers])
    AuthCore-->>Controller: true
    Controller-->>Cliente: 200 OK { mensaje, data }
```

